---
// A starting point for your privacy notice, describing what Events&I itself does with registrations. It is not legal
// advice: fill in the brackets, add anything else your site does, and have it checked for your own situation.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy notice">
	<h1>Privacy notice for event registrations</h1>
	<p><strong>[Your organisation, address and contact]</strong> is responsible for the personal data you give when you register for one of our events.</p>

	<h2>What we keep and why</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Your name and email address, how you will attend, and the sessions or options you choose: to give you a place, send you the joining instructions and calendar invitations, and tell you about changes to the event.</li>
		<li>Your affiliation, any dietary or access needs, and your answer to any question on the form, if you give them: to plan the event.</li>
		<li>Your answers to polls, and any option you suggest: to decide what we do. When you suggest an option, the organisers see your name with it.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>The legal basis is your consent, given when you register. You can change your registration or cancel it at any time with the link in our emails; cancelling deletes it.</p>

	<h2>Who sees it</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Our organisers.</li>
		<li>The host of each session you book, who receives the list of attendees' names, and your email address and affiliation only if you agree to share them. Hosts are asked to delete their lists after the session.</li>
		<li>Cloudflare, which hosts this site and the registration database and checks with Turnstile that the form is filled in by a person, and Resend, which sends our emails, on our behalf. <strong>[Say where the data is stored, for example "in the European Union".]</strong></li>
	</ul>

	<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
	<p>Registrations, poll answers and records of the emails we sent are deleted 30 days after the event. A registration you do not confirm is deleted when its hold lapses, within 48 hours.</p>

	<h2>Your rights</h2>
	<p>You can ask to see, correct or delete your data, or complain to us at <strong>[contact]</strong>. You can also complain to your data protection authority <strong>[in the UK, the Information Commissioner's Office: ico.org.uk]</strong>.</p>

	<p>The registration pages use no tracking or advertising. The form keeps your email address in your browser only to show it on the next page.</p>
</Base>
